  "worked_solution": "In general, congruent polygons have the same shape. In other words:\n\n* they have the same number of sides,\n\n* all corresponding sides are congruent, and\n\n* all corresponding interior angles are congruent.\n\nWith that in mind, let's compare polygons $B$ and $D$ to $A.$\n\n* The polygon $A$ is an octagon (it has $8$ sides). So, the polygons $B$ and $D$ can't be congruent to the polygon $A$ because they do not have $8$ sides.\n\n* On the other hand, $A$ and $C$ have the same shape: they have congruent corresponding sides, and since they are regular polygons, congruent corresponding angles. This implies that $A≅C.$",
